Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(shares): share accounts and who may open a share

The root service now has share accounts (separate from the CasaOS login,
no shell, only for network shares) and can restrict a share to one of
them (ReCasaOS: "share accounts and per-share restriction"). This is the
dashboard side:

- "Share accounts" in Shared Folders: list, add, change password, delete
  (the API refuses deleting an account a share still uses)
- sharing a folder from the file browser asks who may open it: every
  share account, or only one; a shared folder gets "Access" to change it

SambaUsersModal is ported from the ReCasaOS distribution
(ReCasaOS/CasaOS-UI); ShareAccessModal is adapted from it, since every
share is authenticated here (no guest choice, no Time Machine yet).
Stacked on "never ask for an anonymous share".

Co-Authored-By: Gary <contact@ixelia.fr>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
